-- title:
--   Monic polynomial with lower coefficients in mathfrak m_A killing T modulo hS
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$, let $S$ be a commutative $A$-algebra, and let $h, T \in S$. Write $I = hS$ for the ideal generated by $h$ and assume that the quotient $S/hS$ is a finite $A$-module. Assume further that some power of the image of $T$ in $S/hS$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A \cdot (S/hS)$, more precisely that there is $k \in \mathbb N$ with $(T \bmod hS)^k$ in the ideal of $S/hS$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ under the structure map $A \to S/hS$. The conclusion is the existence of a polynomial $P \in A[X]$ which is monic, all of whose coefficients of index $i < \deg P$ lie in $\mathfrak m_A$ (i.e. every non-leading coefficient below the degree lies in the maximal ideal), and which satisfies $P(T) \in hS$, where $P(T)$ denotes the image of $P$ under evaluation at $T$ as an $A$-algebra map $A[X] \to S$.
--
--   This is a Weierstrass-preparation statement in the form obtained from the Cayley–Hamilton theorem for finitely generated modules together with Nakayama's setting: a coordinate $T$ which is nilpotent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ on the finite $A$-module $S/hS$ satisfies a distinguished monic equation modulo $hS$. It is pure commutative algebra and is used in the construction of monic relations on curves, being cited by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_monic_eval2_eq_mul_of_inv_mem_integers_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_monic_eval2_eq_mul_of_inv_mem_integers_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus).
